It joins the ends.

The mind takes something presented as a line and discovers a way to represent it as a wheel.

That is the part that translates beautifully.

Indigo teaches the possibility of a new relation; purple is the relation made perceptible.

Or even:

Indigo teaches the system how to invent purple.

Not literally as visual neuroscience—the metaphor is our abstraction—but operationally that’s the mechanism.

